# Build
target/

# jqwik property-test replay database (regenerated per run)
.jqwik-database

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.classpath
.project
.settings/

# Environment / secrets
.env

# Lighthouse reports. The CI e2e job writes one per public page beside the POM and uploads them as
# build artefacts; they are a measurement of one run, not source. Two of them (1.2 MB of JSON) had
# been committed to the repository root by M6 — with names like `lighthouse--.json`, which is what a
# reader sees first in a portfolio repository.
lighthouse-*.json

# OS / misc
.DS_Store
*.log

# Session scratch — plans, SDD working material, anything an agent left behind.
#
# The CONTENTS are ignored rather than the directory itself (`.superpowers/*`, not
# `.superpowers/`), because git does not descend into an ignored directory and a negation for a file
# inside one therefore never matches. That distinction is the whole reason the exception below
# works.
.superpowers/*

# The one exception: a milestone's hostile-review findings are a deliverable, not scratch. They are
# the record of what the quality gate found and what was done about it, and ENGINEERING_STANDARDS'
# case for a visible PR history applies to them for the same reason.
#
# This exception was missing until M5, so no findings file had ever actually been committed — while
# the M5 worklog entry, three commit messages and PR #8 all stated that it was. A claim in the
# repository that the repository itself contradicts is exactly the defect class this review was
# about, so it is fixed rather than reworded.
!.superpowers/m*-hostile-review-findings.md

# Same reasoning, different artefact: the handoff a session writes for the next one. It is the work
# queue — re-verified findings, each with the failing test to write first — and it is worth more in
# the repository than in a chat log nobody can find again.
!.superpowers/next-session-findings.md

# Playwright MCP scratch output (screenshots, snapshots) from local browser smoke runs.
.playwright-mcp/

# Internal go-to-market material. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. docs/VERMARKTUNG.md is the marketing
# and outreach plan: it names prospects by name, a named academic contact, a partner's separate
# projects and the commercial angle behind each. None of that is portfolio evidence, and all of it
# is damaging in the hands of the people it names.
#
# It is ignored rather than deleted because it is legitimate working material — it simply belongs in
# ~/Work/single-source-of-truth, which is private and is the stated home for strategy and
# positioning. Ignored here so that a `git add .` cannot publish it by accident.
docs/VERMARKTUNG.md
